  "Question": "When simplified, \\(\\log 8\\div\\log\\dfrac18\\) becomes:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\log2\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\log2\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(0\\)",
    "E": "\\(-1\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "For a fixed logarithm base \\(c>0\\), \\(c\\ne1\\), the reciprocal rule gives\n\\[\n\\log\\frac18=\\log(8^{-1})=-\\log8.\n\\]\nBoth arguments are positive, and \\(\\log8\\ne0\\) because \\(8\\ne1\\). Therefore the denominator is nonzero and\n\\[\n\\frac{\\log8}{\\log(1/8)}\n=\\frac{\\log8}{-\\log8}=-1.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
